  "caption": "Quinn's shoulder blade made a crunching noise, so naturally it became a party trick. Then it started aching after long desk days.\n\nThe shoulder blade glides over the ribs with muscle in between. Overhead work, posture and muscle changes can alter that glide and add noise. The noise itself is usually harmless; it's pain or limited function that's worth working on.\n\nWhat often helps: stop clicking it on purpose, strengthen the muscles that steady the shoulder blade, keep your mid-back moving, and ease overhead and reaching load while checking your desk set-up.\n\nIf there's significant pain, weakness, or it started after a fall or fracture, get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
